{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואתנה את הלוים", :translit "v'natati et ha-leviyim", :gloss "and I have given the Levites"} {:he "בני ישראל", :translit "benei yisra'el", :gloss "children of Israel"} {:he "קדש ישראל לה' ראשית, תבואתה", :translit "kodesh yisra'el la' reshit tevu'atah", :gloss "holiness of Israel to YHWH, first, her produce"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 5, :occurrences ["בני ישראל"]} {:kind :other, :note "Five occurrences of 'benei yisra'el' in the verse correspond to five categories: kohanim, leviyim, yisra'elim, gerim, avadim meshuchrarim; linked via Jeremiah 2:3"}], :frame {:text "Jeremiah 2:3 reads קדש ישראל לה' ראשית תבואתה — 'Israel was holiness to YHWH, the first of His produce.' The verse is read as enumerating categories of Israel, which rabbinic tradition expands to include converts (who are called by the name Israel, e.g. Yevamot 47b) and freed slaves (who immerse and join the congregation, Gittin 40b). The Ba'al HaTurim reads the fivefold occurrence of 'benei yisra'el' in Numbers 8:19 as a numerical allusion to all five groups named in Jeremiah 2:3.", :sources ["Jeremiah 2:3" "Yevamot 47b" "Gittin 40b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ולכפר", :translit "u-lichaper", :gloss "and to atone"} {:he "ולכפר על בני ישראל", :translit "u-lichaper al benei yisra'el", :gloss "and to atone upon the children of Israel"} {:he "ואהרן ובניו מקטירים וגו' ולכפר על בני ישראל", :translit "v'aharon u-vanav mak'tirim... u-lichaper al benei yisra'el", :gloss "and Aaron and his sons burn incense... and to atone upon the children of Israel"} {:he "שבועים שבעים נחתך על עמך ולהתם חטאת ולכפר עון", :translit "shavu'im shiv'im nich'tach al am'cha v'la-ketz chatat u-lichaper avon", :gloss "seventy weeks decreed upon your people to finish transgression and to atone iniquity"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ולכפר על בני ישראל" "ולכפר על בני ישראל" "ולכפר עון"]}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that exile atones for sin. At Makkot 24a, Rabbi Yochanan derives from Numbers 14:34 that God gave Israel exile as a mechanism of atonement. Sanhedrin 37b discusses how Galut (banishment/exile) functions as a form of Kaparah. The three Masoretic occurrences of the root כ-פ-ר in atonement contexts — including Daniel 9:24, where ולכפר עון appears in a verse about the decreed exile of 'seventy weeks' — are read by the Ba'al HaTurim as reinforcing the principle that גלות מכפרת, exile itself functions as atonement analogous to a sacrifice.", :sources ["Makkot 24a" "Sanhedrin 37b" "Numbers 14:34" "Daniel 9:24"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 5, :occurrences ["בני ישראל"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "בני ישראל", :refs ["Genesis 32:33" "Genesis 42:5" "Genesis 45:21" "Genesis 46:5" "Genesis 46:8" "Genesis 50:25" "Exodus 1:1" "Exodus 1:9"], :n 502, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Five occurrences of 'benei yisra'el' in the verse correspond to five categories: kohanim, leviyim, yisra'elim, gerim, avadim meshuchrarim; linked via Jeremiah 2:3", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ולכפר על בני ישראל" "ולכפר על בני ישראל" "ולכפר עון"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ולכפר על בני ישראל", :refs ["Numbers 8:19"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ולכפר על בני ישראל", :refs ["Numbers 8:19"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ולכפר עון", :refs ["Daniel 9:24"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:27:49.722000157Z", :model "glm-5.2"}